<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        <a href="/manage/users">Users</a> lists everyone at your company. Search by name, sort any column, and
        select a person to open their profile.
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="Status">
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Active</strong>: they've set a password and can sign in.</li>
            <li><strong>Invite Pending</strong>: they've been invited but haven't set a password yet.</li>
            <li><strong>Locked</strong>: too many wrong passwords. After 5 failed attempts the account locks for
                15 minutes, or you can unlock it straight away from their profile.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Adding someone">
        <ol>
            <li>Select <strong>Register a New User</strong>.</li>
            <li>Enter their <strong>First Name</strong>, <strong>Last Name</strong> and <strong>Email</strong>, and
                choose their <strong>Location(s)</strong>. Managers can only choose locations they have access to.</li>
            <li>Optionally tick <strong>Customize welcome email for this user</strong> to change the subject and
                message for just this person.</li>
            <li>Select <strong>Create User</strong>.</li>
        </ol>
        <FluentText>
            They're emailed a link to set their password, along with your welcome message if onboarding is set
            up. Until they use it, their status is Invite Pending. Use <strong>Resend Invite</strong> on the
            <strong>Account</strong> tab of their profile if the email went missing.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
